// SPI2 with EasyDMA, and the SX1262 on it.
//
// Renode's nRF52840 platform declares spi2 with easyDMA defaulting to false, so
// it models only the legacy register interface. The nRF52840 part the firmware
// drives is SPIM - pointers and counts, not TXD/RXD - so every transfer went
// nowhere and the chip saw not one byte. A peripheral can only be registered
// once at an address, so the script unregisters theirs first.
spi2: SPI.NRF52840_SPI @ sysbus 0x40023000
    easyDMA: true
    -> nvic@0x23

// The chip itself, as the library QEMU loads and a native node links. The port
// is the RF engine's, not a chip server's: there is no longer anything between
// the peripheral and the model.
lora: Radio.VirtualSX1262 @ spi2
    engineHost: "127.0.0.1"
    enginePort: 7777
